<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mastino I della Scala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1277</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mastino I della Scala was the founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scaliger">Scaliger</a> power in Verona. Chosen leader of the commune after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ezzelino-iii-da-romano">Ezzelino III da Romano</a> in 1259, he held the office of captain of the people and was effectively lord of the city by 1262. He was assassinated in 1277, and his brother Alberto I made the lordship hereditary.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mastino-i-della-scala.jpg" alt="Mastino I della Scala" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mikceo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mastino_I_della_Scala.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
